    "section": "disclosures",
    "title": "Anaam sells stake in Wasit Saudi for SAR 38.2M",
    "title_en": null,
    "impact": null,
    "summary": "أعلنت شركة عنام القابضة اليوم، 12 أبريل، أنها قامت ببيع حصتها الكاملة في شركة واسط السعودية للأنظمة الترفيهية والجمالية بمبلغ إجمالي قدره 38.18 مليون ريال. ستتلقى عنام دفعة أولى قدرها 25.2 مليون ريال في غضون 30 يوما من تاريخ توقيع العقد، بينما ستُدفع الدفعة الثانية وقدرها 3.25 مليون ريال بعد عام من توقيع العقد. وتستهدف هذه الصفقة تحسين الحالة المالية لشركة عنام في الربع الثاني من عام 2026."
   },
   {
    "date": "2025-06-25T21:00:00",
    "section": "disclosures",
    "title": "Anaam shareholders reject discharging board members from liability for 2024",
    "title_en": null,
    "impact": null,
    "summary": "Anaam International Holding Group's shareholders disapproved discharging board members from liability for 2024 during the ordinary general meeting held on June 25, 2025, according to a Tadawul statement. They also disapproved appointing an external auditor to review the company’s income statements for Q2, Q3, and Q4 2025, as well as Q1 2026. Additionally, they rejected the auditor's report for 2024 after reviewing it."
   },
   {
    "date": "2025-02-12T21:00:00",
    "section": "disclosures",
    "title": "Anaam shareholders OK reverse stock split to SAR 10; trading suspended for 2 days",
    "title_en": null,
    "impact": null,
    "summary": "Shareholders of Anaam International Holding Group approved a reverse stock split, increasing the nominal share value from SAR 0.50 to SAR 10, during the extraordinary general meeting on February 12. The decision will affect all shareholders of record at the end of the second trading day following the meeting. Trading will be suspended for two days starting February 13, with the suspension expected to be lifted by the end of trading on February 16."
   },
   {
    "date": "2024-08-21T21:00:00",
    "section": "disclosures",
    "title": "Anaam sells hotel for SAR 19.1M",
    "title_en": null,
    "impact": null,
    "summary": "Anaam International Holding Group announced the sale of the Hyatt Al Fursan Hotel in Al Qurayyat, Al-Jouf region to Khaled Mustafa Mohamed Moneim for SAR 19.11 million. The agreement includes all assets and liabilities of the hotel in its current state, with the full value being paid in annual installments. An advance payment of SAR 1.5 million has been agreed upon, and the remaining value of SAR 17.6 million will be paid in four equal annual installments. The deal involves additional securities including mortgages. The aim of the transaction is to finance the company’s activities and enhance liquidity. The hotel was purchased in December 2021 for SAR 16.5 million."
